xodus-service: answer the game's Store questions (licence tokens, its own licence, the Store catalog, what the account
owns, account roles) and give it the player's gamer picture

MetalHorizon 1.0.4, completed in 2.0.0. The engines run Ferestre's xgameruntime (icex/xgameruntime), which asks the service for Store
licence tokens (XML message type 7, XStoreQueryLicenseTokenAsync), the game's own licence (ESDX frames), the Store
catalog (CSDX frames) and the account roles (ASDX frames). This service, from upstream xodus with MetalHorizon's
patches 0002 to 0004, knew none of them: "Unimplemented" and "Unknown magic" in its log, a closed connection for the
game, and in the game no VIP membership, no Car Pass cars and no expansions (MetalHorizon issue #18).

- connection/license.rs: licence tokens the way Ferestre's service (icex/xodus a4f9d5c) asks them, POST
  /v8.0/licenseToken authorized and signed with the title's XSTS token for licensing.mp.microsoft.com, through the
  service's existing XSTS path (xml.rs: xsts_response, factored out of the XSTS branch). Bound to the game's Store ID
  (XODUS_STORE_PRODUCT, binding.rs) when the launcher passes it.
- connection/catalog.rs: Ferestre's Store catalog bridge, plus protocol 2 (MetalHorizon 2.0.0, engine 1.3): the
  request carries flags (1: what the account owns, only) and the answer the products of it the account owns, so the
  in-game store stops pricing what was bought; what is owned is listed even when it is no longer sold on its own. Two
  live tests, ignored by default; one writes the answers engine/tests/store-ownership serves to the runtime.
- connection/collections.rs (2.0.0): what the account owns, from the Store's collections
  (collections.mp.microsoft.com/v6.0/collections/query, as Ferestre's xodus-cli asks it: an MSA device ticket for the
  caller, the user's for the beneficiary), resolved against the public catalog: an add-on counts when its entry names
  the game as its parent, an owned edition or bundle with everything it contains (the VIP membership and the Car Pass
  of a Premium Edition). Kept for ten minutes.
- connection/picture.rs (2.0.0): the gamer picture (GSDX frames): the profile's GameDisplayPicRaw from
  profile.xboxlive.com with the user's Xbox token, fetched as a PNG of the size asked; status 1 when there is none.
  Since 2.1.1 (issue #15: still grey): the address's own format and size are replaced, not repeated, an http address is
  asked over https, and a JPEG (or GIF, WebP, BMP) answer is converted to a PNG of the size asked by macOS's sips.
- connection/router.rs: the frames above; a client closing its connection is no longer logged as an error.
- Cargo.toml: uuid (the collections request's correlation vector), from the workspace.
- xml.rs: the runtime's extended frame size (type bit 0x8000) for requests over 64 KiB; any XML type is answered with
  its type plus one, as the runtime checks.
- proto.rs: the unimplemented protobuf framing refuses instead of panicking.
- main.rs: --latest-version <content id>, the version Microsoft publishes for the game's package (authenticated package
  service, http://update.xboxlive.com), so MetalHorizon can offer an update to an outdated game.
- device.rs: when Microsoft's ticket exchange refuses, the device ticket is renewed once from the stored device key
  (as Ferestre does since icex/xodus e35bde1) and the request tried again, in the service and in --check; the renewed
  ticket stays in memory (nothing written to the Keychain).


